   "history": "Kitfo is attributed to the Gurage people of central Ethiopia — a community celebrated throughout Ethiopia for their hospitality and their food. The Gurage prepare kitfo with enormous care: the beef is minced or hand-chopped, never mechanically processed, then mixed with mitmita-infused kibbeh and mekelesha (a fragrant spice blend) until uniformly and perfectly seasoned. It is served in three ways: raw (leb-leb), warmed (leb-leb), or fully cooked (be-kibbeh). Kitfo with ayib and gomen is one of the great Ethiopian meal combinations."
