   "history": "The Afar are a nomadic pastoralist people living in one of the world's most extreme environments — the Afar Triangle, which includes the Danakil Depression (the hottest place on earth). Their cuisine is entirely adapted to nomadic life: camel and goat meat, camel milk, dates, and dried foods that can be transported. Hilib Ari (camel meat stew) is the most prestigious Afar dish — camel meat is expensive and valued, prepared for weddings, religious celebrations, and important guests. The Afar use a spice mixture called berbere that differs significantly from Amhara berbere, featuring more cumin and coriander."
