   "history": "Ethiopia is one of humanity's most ancient food civilizations — the birthplace of coffee, of teff, of injera fermentation, of the Ethiopian Orthodox fasting tradition that produced the world's most extensive plant-based culinary heritage. Ethiopian food is 3,000 years in the making: the ancient Aksumite trade routes carried Ethiopian spices to Arabia and India; the Ethiopian Orthodox church shaped a 200+ day annual plant-based eating tradition; the Kaffa forest gave the world its most beloved drink; the highland farmers of the Amhara region perfected the berbere-kibbeh-injera trinity that defines the national cuisine. This Heritage Platter assembles the complete story — from the ancient to the modern, from the highlands to the lowlands, from the fasting to the feast."
