   "history": "Maharagwe ya Nazi is a cornerstone of Swahili coastal cuisine, born from centuries of Indian Ocean trade that brought spices, coconuts, and culinary traditions from Arabia, India, and Persia to East Africa. Along Kenya's coast, where coconut palms line the shoreline and coconut cream is a daily cooking staple, this creamy bean stew has nourished families for generations. It is affordable, deeply nutritious, and beloved for the way coconut milk transforms humble beans into something extraordinary.",
