   "history": "Mandazi originated along the Kenyan coast as part of the rich Swahili food culture shaped by centuries of Indian Ocean trade. The use of coconut milk and cardamom reflects the spice trade routes that connected East Africa with Arabia, Persia, and the Indian subcontinent. From coastal homes to inland towns, mandazi spread across Kenya through migration, trade, and cultural exchange until it became one of the most recognisable everyday foods in the country.",
