   "history": "Viazi Karai is one of the most iconic street foods of the Kenyan coast, born from the profound influence of Indian cuisine on Swahili food culture. The technique of coating food in spiced gram flour batter and deep-frying it came to East Africa through centuries of Indian Ocean trade and the settlement of Indian communities along the coast. In Mombasa, viazi karai vendors have been a fixture of the Old Town streets and evening markets for generations, frying fresh batches throughout the day.",
