   "origin": "Swahili Coast — influenced by Arab and Persian skewered meat traditions",
   "history": "Mishkaki traces its origins to the Swahili Coast, where centuries of Arab and Persian trade introduced the tradition of marinated skewered meat to East Africa. The word mishkaki itself is derived from Arabic. Over generations the dish spread inland and became one of the most universally beloved street foods across Kenya — found at roadside charcoal grills from Nairobi to Kisumu, always smoky, always fragrant with spice.",
