   "history": "Uji wa Wimbi — finger millet porridge — is one of the oldest foods in East African history. Finger millet (wimbi) has been cultivated in the African highlands for thousands of years and was a primary cereal crop long before maize arrived from the Americas. In Kenyan households across every community, uji has served as the first food given to weaning infants, the breakfast of farmers heading to the fields before dawn, and the comfort of the elderly. It is a food that connects generations.",
