  "desc": "Uji wa Wimbi is Kenya's most universally consumed breakfast — a warm, smooth, nourishing porridge made from finger millet flour. Slightly earthy, mildly nutty, and deeply comforting, it is the first food of infants and the morning ritual of millions of Kenyan households.",
  "longDesc": "There is almost no food more universally Kenyan than a cup of Uji wa Wimbi in the morning. From Nairobi apartments to rural homesteads in the Rift Valley, from coastal towns to highland farms, the sight of a pot of dark, steaming finger millet porridge on the stove is the smell of a Kenyan morning beginning. Finger millet — wimbi — is one of the oldest cereal crops in Africa, and its transformation into warm, smooth porridge is one of the continent's most enduring culinary traditions.",
