   "history": "Managu (African nightshade, Solanum nigrum) is one of the oldest and most nutritious indigenous vegetables in Kenya. It has been gathered from homestead gardens and wild patches across the country for generations, prized for its distinctive slightly bitter flavour that mellows with cooking and for its exceptional nutritional density.",
