   "history": "Mabuyu are the seeds of the baobab tree (Adansonia digitata), coated in a spiced, coloured sugar syrup and eaten as a sweet snack. They have been sold by coastal vendors in Mombasa for generations, the seeds cracking open to reveal a slightly tart, fibrous pulp beneath the sweet candy coating. They are one of the most distinctively Swahili of all Kenyan sweets — and one of the most ancient.",
