   "origin": "National — the most complete expression of Kenya's grain heritage",
   "history": "Mixed grain uji is the culmination of Kenya's extraordinary cereal diversity. Finger millet, sorghum, maize, and sometimes pearl millet are combined in varying proportions by different communities, creating a porridge that draws on the nutritional strengths of each grain. The practice of blending grains is ancient — Kenyan communities understood intuitively that a combination of grains produced a more complete, nutritious, and flavourful porridge than any single grain alone. This is KEN200 — the 200th recipe in the Kenyan collection on GieesK Recipes — a fitting celebration of the breadth and depth of Kenyan culinary heritage.",
