  "culturalNote": "Sabaayad is a beloved everyday bread throughout Somalia, its flaky layers reflecting culinary techniques shared across the wider Horn of Africa and South Asian trading world. It travels under several names — jabaati, borrowed from the Swahili chapati, and also kimis and ceesh — and Somali sources use them interchangeably for this one bread. The borrowed name is a little misleading: despite being called chapati, it is laminated and layered, so it is closer to a paratha than to an Indian chapati.",
