   "history": "Samaki wa Kupaka is the fish equivalent of Kuku wa Kupaka — a whole snapper or kingfish marinated in Zanzibar spices, grilled over charcoal, and repeatedly basted with coconut-tamarind sauce until magnificently lacquered. It is the signature fish dish of Zanzibar and one of the most celebrated seafood preparations in East Africa. The Forodhani Gardens night market is famous for it.",
