   "history": "Urojo is Zanzibar's most complex and celebrated street food — a sour, tangy soup made from a mango-coconut broth, served with a bewildering array of toppings: bhajias, mishkaki, kachori, cassava chips, boiled eggs, and a drizzle of peanut-chilli sauce. It is the food that defines Zanzibar's Stone Town evenings — eaten standing at the Forodhani Gardens as the sun sets over the Indian Ocean. No two vendors' urojo is identical; each guards their recipe fiercely."
