   "origin": "Haya people of Kagera region, northwestern Tanzania — the Great Lakes banana civilisation",
   "history": "The Haya (Wahaya) people of the Kagera region around Bukoba are one of East Africa's great banana civilisations — their fertile land between the Kagera River and Lake Victoria produces exceptional bananas and plantains. The Haya Matoke (steamed plantain stew) is distinct from Uganda's version — cooked with peanuts, smoked fish, and local vegetables in a preparation that reflects the agricultural wealth of the region. The Haya kingdom was one of the most sophisticated pre-colonial states in East Africa."
