   "origin": "Hadzabe (Hadza) people of Lake Eyasi, Arusha region — one of the oldest peoples on earth",
   "history": "The Hadzabe (Hadza) are one of the world's last true hunter-gatherer communities — a people of approximately 1,000—1,300 individuals living around Lake Eyasi in the Arusha region who still hunt with bows and arrows and gather wild plants, berries, and honey. Genetic evidence suggests the Hadza are one of the most ancient population lineages on earth, with cultural and linguistic connections extending back at least 100,000 years. Their food system is based entirely on what the immediate environment provides — no farming, no herding, no storage. Every meal is hunted or gathered fresh.",
